WEBVTT

00:00.520 --> 00:04.062
Thank you for your patience, everyone. This morning and I will confirm that we are

00:04.086 --> 00:06.170
recording and live streaming on the town's website.

00:07.830 --> 00:10.886
Chair Ash, the time is now 10:00 and I can confirm

00:10.918 --> 00:14.290
that this meeting is being recorded and webcast on the town's website.

00:26.680 --> 00:30.536
Public hearings are held in a hybrid format with members of committee and

00:30.568 --> 00:34.416
the audience attending, both in person in the council chambers,

00:34.608 --> 00:38.000
as well as electronically using a Zoom

00:38.040 --> 00:41.024
webinar. The video from this meeting is being live,

00:41.072 --> 00:43.608
webcast, and recorded for future viewing.

00:43.744 --> 00:47.016
Displayed on the screen is the electronic meeting etiquette

00:47.168 --> 00:50.420
to be followed by those addressing committee electronically.

00:50.970 --> 00:54.474
For any individual watching the webcast who is interested in providing

00:54.522 --> 00:57.470
comments on applications being considered today,

00:57.810 --> 01:01.594
please visit www. Dot Bracebridge Dot CA

01:01.762 --> 01:05.354
to view the participation details and link contained in

01:05.362 --> 01:08.986
the meeting agenda. The following maximum time limits

01:09.058 --> 01:12.522
are applicable. The applicant and or their agent may

01:12.546 --> 01:15.030
make a presentation of up to ten minutes.

01:15.610 --> 01:19.870
Members of the public may also make a presentation of up to five minutes

01:20.600 --> 01:24.952
when instructed to do so by the chair. Members of the public who are participating

01:25.016 --> 01:28.720
electronically should click the raise hand button in Zoom

01:28.760 --> 01:32.480
to indicate their desire to speak. Those calling into the meeting

01:32.520 --> 01:36.456
by telephone are to press nine on your device to raise your electronic

01:36.488 --> 01:39.792
hand. Members participating in person will

01:39.816 --> 01:42.980
be recognized by the chair and invited to the microphone.

01:44.000 --> 01:47.512
Any disrespectful, inappropriate or derogatory behavior

01:47.616 --> 01:51.740
may result in expulsion from the meeting in accordance with section 241

01:51.800 --> 01:55.080
two of the municipal act. Thank you, chair Ash.

01:55.940 --> 01:59.404
Thank you very much. I realized I didn't have my microphone on at the beginning,

01:59.452 --> 02:03.116
so. Yes, this is the town of Bracebridge. Committee of Adjustment hearing

02:03.228 --> 02:06.716
for August 9. Moving ahead, does any member have

02:06.748 --> 02:09.960
a pecuniary interest on any matter being discussed today?

02:10.540 --> 02:14.156
No, seeing none. Thank you. I will

02:14.188 --> 02:17.228
provide the land. Acknowledgement. We want to acknowledge that

02:17.244 --> 02:21.332
we are on lands traditionally occupied by indigenous peoples. They continue to

02:21.356 --> 02:25.288
care for this land. They continue to shape bracelets today, and we want

02:25.304 --> 02:28.800
to show our respect hundreds of years after the first

02:28.840 --> 02:32.656
treaties were signed, they remain relevant today in guiding

02:32.688 --> 02:34.540
our decisions and actions.

02:36.080 --> 02:39.540
So I'm looking for minutes of the previous meeting.

02:40.400 --> 02:43.680
Do we have. Are those on the agenda for today

02:43.760 --> 02:47.208
to move in second? Okay. Do I have a mover and a

02:47.224 --> 02:50.526
seconder for the minutes? I would so

02:50.558 --> 02:54.390
move. Thank you. Do we have the seconder? I will second. Thank you very much.

02:54.430 --> 02:57.966
All in favor? The minutes are approved. That was a

02:58.158 --> 03:02.130
motion made by member Beaumont and seconded by member Franklin.

03:03.670 --> 03:07.010
Are there any requests for withdrawal or deferral?

03:11.190 --> 03:14.902
Thank you, chair Ash. There have been no requests for withdrawal

03:14.926 --> 03:18.484
or deferral. Thank you very much and could you please advise how the notice of

03:18.492 --> 03:22.324
the public hearings were circulated? Notices for the minor variance

03:22.372 --> 03:25.828
applications were sent by first class mail to the assessed owners

03:25.884 --> 03:29.572
within 60 meters of the properties and

03:29.596 --> 03:32.844
to those persons and agencies likely to have an interest in

03:32.852 --> 03:36.412
the applications. The notices were provided a minimum

03:36.436 --> 03:40.420
of ten days prior to this meeting in accordance with the provisions of the Planning

03:40.460 --> 03:44.086
act. Persons wishing to receive notice of the decision of

03:44.118 --> 03:47.950
committee must submit a written request to the Secretary treasurer by

03:47.990 --> 03:50.690
email to planningeracebridge, CA.

03:52.390 --> 03:55.662
Thank you very much. We will now hold the public

03:55.726 --> 03:59.890
hearing for application D 1321 24

04:00.310 --> 04:03.614
by 689-1535 Canada,

04:03.702 --> 04:06.870
Inc. And Miss Peters, can you provide a quick

04:06.910 --> 04:10.148
summary of the application please? Thank you

04:10.204 --> 04:33.156
chair ash this

04:33.188 --> 04:36.148
minor variance application was considered by the committee in July.

04:36.244 --> 04:40.082
However, after that hearing, a a landowner near the subject property

04:40.146 --> 04:43.674
advised staff that they had not received a copy of the public notice in

04:43.682 --> 04:46.882
the mail. Upon further investigation, it was found that there

04:46.906 --> 04:51.506
was an error made when generating the mailing list for the circulation as

04:51.538 --> 04:54.938
set out in item seven of the staff report. While posting the sign on the

04:54.954 --> 04:58.314
property and posting the notice for that July hearing

04:58.362 --> 05:01.994
on the town's website would have satisfied the planning act circulation

05:02.082 --> 05:05.698
requirements, staff determined that recirculation was appropriate in

05:05.714 --> 05:09.418
order to ensure that the town's standard practices for public notification

05:09.474 --> 05:13.154
were consistently applied. As not all of the committee members

05:13.242 --> 05:16.714
here today were present at the July 8 hearing, I will provide

05:16.762 --> 05:19.910
a full presentation while keeping it as brief as possible.

05:21.730 --> 05:25.750
The subject lands are located at 76 covered bridge trail.

05:27.690 --> 05:31.866
The minor variance application was submitted in order to change the way lot frontage

05:31.898 --> 05:35.298
is measured for certain lots within a draft plan of subdivision and

05:35.314 --> 05:38.642
to exempt one lot from the minimum setback for a driveway

05:38.706 --> 05:42.866
to interior side lot lines. Specifically, the applicant

05:42.898 --> 05:47.178
is requesting that the following definition of lot frontage apply to proposed lots

05:47.234 --> 05:50.590
8935, 36, and 38.

05:50.890 --> 05:54.626
Lot frontage shall be measured along the front lot line except

05:54.658 --> 05:58.226
where multiple lot lines above a street or where the side lot lines are not

05:58.258 --> 06:02.066
parallel, in which case the lot frontage is to be measured as a distance

06:02.098 --> 06:06.378
of 6 meters at a distance of 6 meters or 19.7ft

06:06.474 --> 06:09.802
back from the straight line cord where the two side lot lines meet the

06:09.826 --> 06:13.650
lot lines abutting the street. The applicant is also requesting that

06:13.690 --> 06:17.458
section 5.10, subsection four of comprehensive

06:17.514 --> 06:21.082
zoning bylaw 20 1688 not apply to

06:21.106 --> 06:24.858
proposed lot 36. This zoning bylaw provision

06:24.914 --> 06:28.538
requires a driveway to be set back a minimum of 1.2

06:28.594 --> 06:32.428
meters or 3.9ft from any interior side lot line

06:32.554 --> 06:36.136
except on a lot with a frontage of less than 8 meters where adjoining

06:36.168 --> 06:39.832
driveways are permitted. The overall minor variance sketch

06:39.856 --> 06:43.240
is shown here. On this slide

06:43.320 --> 06:47.312
is an enlargement showing proposed lots eight and nine with the alternative

06:47.376 --> 06:49.260
frontage measurements shown,

06:50.440 --> 06:53.072
and this enlargement shows lots 35,

06:53.136 --> 06:56.580
36, and 38 with the alternative frontages shown.

06:59.810 --> 07:03.202
Some relevant background information on this property is that

07:03.226 --> 07:07.434
a rezoning application was received by the town in 2011 and

07:07.482 --> 07:10.786
associated applications for draft plan of subdivision approval and

07:10.818 --> 07:14.562
draft plan of condominium approval were submitted to the District of Muskoka

07:14.586 --> 07:18.522
at that time. The applications were updated in 2019

07:18.706 --> 07:22.018
and a concurrent public meeting for consideration of the three

07:22.074 --> 07:25.786
planning applications was held jointly by the town and district.

07:25.978 --> 07:29.474
The minutes of that meeting are available online through a link in the staff

07:29.522 --> 07:33.194
report. The applications were deferred at that time

07:33.282 --> 07:36.978
to allow for consideration of comments received at the public meeting and until

07:37.034 --> 07:40.442
any items identified in the peer reviews of technical reports had been

07:40.466 --> 07:43.730
addressed. The applications were subsequently

07:43.770 --> 07:47.466
appealed to the Ontario Land Tribunal in 2022

07:47.618 --> 07:51.288
due to lack of decision within the statutory timelines.

07:51.474 --> 07:54.900
Through the appeal process, a settlement was reached and was accepted by

07:54.940 --> 07:58.692
the Ontario Land Tribunal with a final decision issued in October

07:58.756 --> 08:02.252
2023. The OLT decision includes

08:02.316 --> 08:06.460
conditions of draft approval for the plan of subdivision and common element condominium,

08:06.580 --> 08:10.012
as well as a site specific zoning bylaw applicable to the

08:10.036 --> 08:12.960
subject property. The decision can be viewed online.

08:13.700 --> 08:17.340
Differences between the draft plan of subdivision referenced in the OLT

08:17.380 --> 08:21.194
decision and the draft of survey plan of the Plan of subdivision

08:21.242 --> 08:24.802
for final approval have resulted in certain proposed lots not meeting

08:24.866 --> 08:28.594
the minimum frontage requirement. The variance related to

08:28.602 --> 08:32.306
the driveway setback is an administrative correction. It does appear

08:32.338 --> 08:36.298
that this was inadvertently omitted from the zoning bylaw prepared by OLt,

08:36.434 --> 08:40.442
and staff would note that the online version of that decision does include

08:40.506 --> 08:43.634
lot 36 in the list of proposed lots to be exempt

08:43.682 --> 08:46.838
from the driveway setback. However, the PDF version that

08:46.854 --> 08:51.742
the town received does not the

08:51.766 --> 08:55.542
subject property is currently vacant. The interior of the property is

08:55.566 --> 08:59.022
well treed and mainly flat. The property abuts the

08:59.046 --> 09:02.438
Beaver creek and contains slopes along the north,

09:02.534 --> 09:05.490
south and east portions down to the creek.

09:08.790 --> 09:12.206
These are some photos of the subject lands. The top photos

09:12.278 --> 09:15.390
show a view into the property from the street and

09:15.470 --> 09:18.822
the opposite view out toward the street along what would be the

09:18.846 --> 09:22.302
proposed entrance way into the development. The bottom photos are

09:22.326 --> 09:26.006
views along covered bridge trail to the north and south of the entrance

09:26.038 --> 09:27.290
to the subject lands.

09:31.270 --> 09:34.966
The subject lands are designated residential within the urban

09:34.998 --> 09:38.918
center designation of the town of Bracebridge. Official plan a

09:38.934 --> 09:43.158
number of relevant official plan policies are set out in the staff report in items

09:43.214 --> 09:46.606
31 through 36, they emphasize that the majority

09:46.638 --> 09:50.366
of residential growth shall be directed to the urban center to utilize

09:50.438 --> 09:53.886
full municipal services, that an emphasis should be placed on growth

09:53.958 --> 09:57.134
within the built up area as identified in the official plan

09:57.262 --> 10:00.662
and that a mix of housing types at varying densities, tenure,

10:00.726 --> 10:04.048
and affordability should be provided. Staff are of the

10:04.064 --> 10:07.880
opinion that the requested variances, which would enable the development to proceed

10:07.920 --> 10:11.500
as planned, meet the general intent of the town's official plan.

10:14.840 --> 10:17.976
The property is zoned residential type four special

10:18.048 --> 10:22.136
35 in part, residential type four special 36 in part,

10:22.288 --> 10:25.792
environmental protection one in part and open space one

10:25.896 --> 10:29.980
in part. According to comprehensive zoning bylaw 20 1688,

10:30.280 --> 10:33.456
the zone schedule included in the OLT decision is shown here,

10:33.568 --> 10:36.700
with the innermost area, which is outlined in red,

10:37.040 --> 10:40.656
being the r 435 zone where buildings and

10:40.688 --> 10:44.256
driveways would be located. The r 435

10:44.328 --> 10:48.328
special provisions include a reduced lot frontage of 7 meters

10:48.384 --> 10:51.680
for end unit road dwellings, a reduced front yard

10:51.720 --> 10:54.180
setback of 6 meters for road dwellings,

10:54.600 --> 10:58.058
and that section 510, subsection four of the

10:58.074 --> 11:01.630
zoning bylaw does not apply to lots eight, nine, and 35.

11:02.090 --> 11:06.338
As noted, there has also been a variance request to

11:06.474 --> 11:10.482
exempt lot 36 from that driveway setback provision, and the online version

11:10.506 --> 11:13.150
of the decision does include lot 36.

11:14.450 --> 11:17.922
The proposed change to the lot frontage definition would result in

11:17.946 --> 11:21.710
all of the proposed lots meeting the minimum lot frontage requirements.

11:22.050 --> 11:26.122
Alternate lot frontage definitions have been used in previous subdivision developments

11:26.186 --> 11:29.730
for similar reasons of irregularly shaped lots, and staff

11:29.770 --> 11:32.738
are of the opinion that this approach is sound and that the development as a

11:32.754 --> 11:35.826
whole will not be negatively impacted by the variance.

11:36.018 --> 11:39.042
Staff are of the opinion that the variances meet the general intent of the zoning

11:39.066 --> 11:39.830
bylaw.

11:42.370 --> 11:45.946
The proposed development has received approval through an OLt decision,

11:46.018 --> 11:50.138
and the variances will facilitate the development of a historically vacant property

11:50.194 --> 11:53.630
with a medium density housing form that will increase the housing stock

11:53.710 --> 11:57.694
within the town's urban center on full municipal services. Staff are

11:57.702 --> 12:01.414
of the opinion that the variances are desirable for the appropriate development or use of

12:01.422 --> 12:05.254
the land. The variances to the lot

12:05.302 --> 12:09.094
frontage definition for specific proposed lots are not anticipated

12:09.142 --> 12:13.054
to have any negative impact on properties abutting the subject lands. On future

12:13.102 --> 12:17.330
abutting lots within the proposed subdivision or on covered bridge trail,

12:17.760 --> 12:21.952
the development will require satisfying conditions of draft approval that

12:21.976 --> 12:25.800
will result in development agreements prior to the construction of dwellings

12:25.840 --> 12:29.272
and driveways, ensuring a further opportunity for staff to

12:29.296 --> 12:33.016
provide feedback to the developer and ensure that each proposed lot has safe and

12:33.048 --> 12:35.380
appropriate access to the internal road.

12:36.640 --> 12:39.952
As noted, the variance request related to the driveway setback on

12:39.976 --> 12:43.232
lot 36 is an administrative correction and upholds

12:43.256 --> 12:46.588
the intent of the OLT decision. It is the opinion of staff that

12:46.604 --> 12:48.360
the variances are minor in nature.

12:51.380 --> 12:54.636
Comments received from the town's public works department indicate no

12:54.668 --> 12:56.960
concerns with the minor variance application.

12:58.260 --> 13:02.300
Comments in opposition to the application were received from Ilmar

13:02.340 --> 13:05.972
Kentz of 184 covered bridge trail prior to

13:05.996 --> 13:10.204
the July 8 hearing. The concerns noted include traffic

13:10.252 --> 13:13.754
levels on covered bridge trail, a potential parking lot on the subject

13:13.802 --> 13:17.082
property near covered bridge trail, the suitability of the

13:17.106 --> 13:20.458
ground for construction, the style of the proposed, and the

13:20.474 --> 13:24.218
style of the proposed dwellings being suited for a city rather than for

13:24.234 --> 13:28.378
the town of Bracebridge. As a brief response, staff would note

13:28.394 --> 13:32.402
that several studies were submitted with the applications for rezoning,

13:32.506 --> 13:36.138
draft plan of subdivision approval, and draft plan of condominium

13:36.194 --> 13:39.290
approval, including a traffic brief, slope stability

13:39.370 --> 13:42.626
study, and geotechnical report, and these studies were

13:42.658 --> 13:45.710
all part of the appeal package provided to the OLT.

13:46.690 --> 13:50.458
Staff are not aware of any plans for a centralized visitor parking area

13:50.554 --> 13:54.498
on the subject lands. A draft grading plan is attached to

13:54.514 --> 13:57.706
the staff report to provide the general layout

13:57.778 --> 14:01.258
of the proposed development and the external

14:01.434 --> 14:05.050
appearance of the proposed dwellings is not germane to the variance

14:05.090 --> 14:08.330
requests, which are for lot frontage and driveway setbacks.

14:09.630 --> 14:13.310
No further comments. Public comments were received either prior

14:13.350 --> 14:17.130
to the July 8 hearing or prior to this hearing

14:17.470 --> 14:20.530
and no supporting documents were submitted with the application.

14:23.430 --> 14:27.406
Should the committee approve the application, staff would recommend the following condition

14:27.598 --> 14:31.118
that the minor variance sketch in Appendix A of the staff

14:31.174 --> 14:35.180
report be attached to the decision and that the configuration of lots

14:35.220 --> 14:38.932
8935, 36, and 38 be in

14:38.956 --> 14:40.480
accordance with that sketch.

14:43.060 --> 14:46.660
In conclusion, as set out more fully in the staff report and subject

14:46.700 --> 14:50.332
to the recommended conditions, staff are of the opinion that the variances could be

14:50.356 --> 14:54.124
deemed to meet the four tests of a minor variance and that concludes my presentation.

14:54.172 --> 14:56.996
Chair Ash thank you very much Miss Peters.

14:57.108 --> 14:59.940
Committee members, any questions for Miss Petersen?

15:00.550 --> 15:03.726
No, seeing none. Okay, thank you and I will turn

15:03.758 --> 15:07.230
it over to the committee clerk to bring on the applicant

15:07.270 --> 15:10.910
or agent. Thank you. The applicant or their agent

15:10.950 --> 15:14.462
are reminded to use the raise hand button in Zoom to be brought into

15:14.486 --> 15:17.822
the meeting, and I do see that Andrew has raised his hand.

15:17.886 --> 15:19.930
Andrew, I will now add you to the meeting.

15:36.320 --> 15:39.840
Welcome to the meeting, Andrew. We ask that you please turn on your video and

15:39.880 --> 15:43.536
your microphone, state your full name with your mailing address,

15:43.608 --> 15:46.620
including your postal code, and then you may begin your comments.

15:49.640 --> 15:53.412
Good morning, madam chair and committee members. Can everybody hear me? Yes,

15:53.436 --> 15:57.332
we can. My name is Andrew Pascuzzo. I am a registered professional

15:57.396 --> 16:01.028
planner. My address is 173 St.

16:01.084 --> 16:03.836
Marie street in Collingwood, Ontario.

16:04.028 --> 16:07.092
L, nine, Y, three, k, four.

16:07.276 --> 16:10.540
I am here this morning representing the

16:10.580 --> 16:15.320
numbered company, the Canada, Inc. Numbered company, which was referenced previously.

16:15.740 --> 16:19.700
Obviously, my client has had a fairly lengthy approval

16:19.740 --> 16:22.944
process. We've already received

16:23.072 --> 16:26.872
approval for this minor variance and understand that there

16:26.896 --> 16:29.260
was an administrative error.

16:29.920 --> 16:33.728
I would like to thank Kelly for her very detailed

16:33.784 --> 16:37.512
presentation and assistance throughout the

16:37.536 --> 16:41.552
process here. She hit a home run on our presentation again,

16:41.696 --> 16:45.104
so I'm not going to say much here. I would just.

16:45.232 --> 16:48.360
Obviously, I'm asking for the committee again to approve

16:48.400 --> 16:52.254
the minor variance application. It is my professional opinion

16:52.302 --> 16:55.170
that the minor variance meets the four tests.

16:56.030 --> 16:59.990
The reason for the request is because of the irregular

17:00.110 --> 17:03.838
shape of the proposed lots, as well as the site itself,

17:04.014 --> 17:07.050
which sits on a peninsula around the river.

17:08.310 --> 17:11.590
Yeah, so that's basically all I have to say.

17:11.670 --> 17:14.886
My client is obviously. And his consulting team

17:14.918 --> 17:18.534
is proceeding through to satisfy the conditions of draft

17:18.582 --> 17:21.938
approval because he would like to move ahead with

17:22.034 --> 17:24.890
construction as soon as possible on the property.

17:24.930 --> 17:28.058
So if there are any questions, I'm more than happy to

17:28.154 --> 17:31.842
respond. I'm also here to listen to any comments from

17:31.906 --> 17:36.010
additional neighbors that may have been caught within the recirculation.

17:36.170 --> 17:39.426
Thank you very much, madam chair. Thank you very much,

17:39.458 --> 17:43.010
Andrew. Committee members, any questions at this time? No,

17:43.090 --> 17:46.362
we don't have any questions for you right now, so if you

17:46.386 --> 17:49.120
want to hang back, that's great.

17:52.660 --> 17:56.244
We'll now look for member or comments from the public.

17:56.372 --> 18:00.320
Are you here to speak to this application?

18:00.980 --> 18:04.320
No, you're just here to listen. Okay, thank you very much.

18:04.780 --> 18:08.516
Then we can proceed to members who might be available on

18:08.548 --> 18:11.636
Zoom. Thank you. And, chair Ash, I can confirm

18:11.668 --> 18:15.440
that we have no members of the public attending the meeting by Zoom.

18:16.790 --> 18:20.438
Thank you very much. That will conclude.

18:20.614 --> 18:24.198
Any further questions from the committee that you want to ask?

18:24.334 --> 18:28.490
No, thank you. All right.

18:30.590 --> 18:34.638
Could you please put the recommended, the recommendation by staff up

18:34.654 --> 18:37.366
on the screen for us? Thank you. Thank you, chair Ash. One moment,

18:37.398 --> 18:37.970
please.

18:50.920 --> 18:54.744
So there. We have the recommendation as provided by staff.

18:54.832 --> 18:57.940
I am looking for a motion on this application,

18:58.400 --> 19:02.112
member Beaumont. Chair, I would move that

19:02.136 --> 19:06.080
we accept this minor variance with the conditions supplied

19:06.120 --> 19:09.672
by staff. Thank you very much. Do I have a seconder for that?

19:09.856 --> 19:13.432
I'll second it. Thank you, member Franklin. All those in

19:13.456 --> 19:16.976
favor? All in favor? Your application has

19:17.008 --> 19:21.048
been approved, Andrew, with the stated condition. Thank you

19:21.064 --> 19:21.940
very much.

19:23.840 --> 19:27.768
And I'll now declare this public hearing

19:27.944 --> 19:31.824
concluded. And that is

19:31.872 --> 19:35.200
it. I'm looking for a motion to adjourn.

19:36.780 --> 19:41.044
Thank you, member Franklin. Thank you, member Beaumont.

19:41.132 --> 19:43.940
All in favor? We're adjourned. Thank you very much.
